@dugramen 
I have created a sample video to demonstrate Unity's approach to handling large, complex data structures. Here it is:

I have translated the script I wrote into a GDScript-like syntax for clearer understanding.

Original Script:
```csharp
public class Main : MonoBehaviour
{
    [SerializeField] private int _intValue;
    [SerializeField] private string _stringValue;
    [SerializeField] private int[] _intArray;
    [SerializeField] private Vector3 _vector3Value;
    [SerializeField] private UnityEngine.Object _objectValue;
    [SerializeField] private MyStruct[] _myStructArray;


    [Serializable]
    public struct MyStruct
    {
        [SerializeField] private int _intValue;
        [SerializeField] private string _stringValue;
        [SerializeField] private int[] _intArray;
        [SerializeField] private Vector3 _vector3Value;
        [SerializeField] private UnityEngine.Object _objectValue;
    }

}
```

> As Godot doesn't have struct yet, I'm using Resource as an alternative

GDScript-like syntax:
```gdscript
class_name Main extends Node

@export var int_value: int
@export var string_value: String
@export var int_array: PackedInt32Array
@export var vector3_value: Vector3
@export var object_value: Resource
@export var my_struct_array: Array[MyStruct]


class MyStruct extends Resource:
    @export var int_value: int
    @export var string_value: String
    @export var int_array: PackedInt32Array
    @export var vector3_value: Vector3
    @export var object_value: Resource
```

